Titlebar: no title, three centered controls (Back, Rotate, Create)

Owner design: the window title is hidden and three small rounded-rectangle buttons with a hairline border (brighter under the pointer) sit centered in the titlebar: Back (KEYCODE_BACK), Rotate (View > Girar / Cmd+R) and Create (a menu of the Arquivo share targets: new post, story, reel, message from Mac files). Glyphs are drawn into one 16x16 template box so the buttons match. The MacApkTitlebarButton/MacApkTitlebarTarget classes sit in a hunk shared with earlier changes; runtime.patch carries them.

diff --git a/runtime/src/cocoa_bridge.mm b/runtime/src/cocoa_bridge.mm
--- a/runtime/src/cocoa_bridge.mm
+++ b/runtime/src/cocoa_bridge.mm
@@ -10007,48 +11072,77 @@ static void InstallBackTitlebarAccessory(NSWindow* w) {
         return !e || std::strcmp(e, "0") != 0;
     }();
     if (!on) return;
-    MacApkBackAccessory* acc = [[MacApkBackAccessory alloc] init];
